COMMERCIAL S11.2-R15 CANONICAL REBIND DIAGNOSIS

Date: 2026-09-23
Scope: source-only, before any R15 server mutation

Observed state

- Canonical Application main is 77f9079956a42ee411e17f5697da96f6810ba966
  with tree 370001f8ce0491ddf7709c2cee16d452d6098721.
- Canonical Control control-main is 7c634d3b82572e8459d51c69f04dce82c624d766
  with tree 1bfbd80d5478dd24f8f3e47d3654a8b7dea649e4.
- The authoritative R14.1 freeze resolves to that Control commit.
- Both canonical CI runs are GREEN and both server worktrees are clean.
- P0_RECOVERY is closed and the R14.1 technical runtime latency profile is GREEN.
- The deployable S11.2 controller still binds its source precondition and target
  freeze to the earlier bootstrap release.  Running it unchanged against the
  R14.1 runtime would correctly stop with repository/freeze drift before backup.

Classification

EXPECTED_RELEASE_BINDING_DRIFT_AFTER_R14_1

Resolution

- Rebind only the existing backup-first S11.2 controller to the current
  canonical Application and Control source state.
- Keep the already reviewed S11 product, migration, synthetic journey,
  admission-cap, provenance, fallback and promotion contracts unchanged.
- Create a new annotated R15 freeze after merge with exact Application and
  Control commit/tree provenance.
- Require the controller to make the full backup before it switches either
  server repository to the target release.

Second predeploy finding

- The live singleton is intentionally fail-closed at
  `S11_DISABLED|CANARY_RED` from the earlier bounded recovery attempts.
- Migration 0033 makes a started Canary epoch immutable and treats a terminal
  state as final.  The R15 controller therefore cannot legitimately reuse that
  epoch or reset its timestamps in place.
- Deploying the first R15 rebind unchanged would create the verified backup and
  then stop at `S11_2_EXISTING_CANARY_STATE_RED`; no partial activation would be
  accepted.

Bounded source correction

- Application PR #119 adds migration 0034.  It archives exactly one terminal
  epoch before rearming the singleton to `S11_DISABLED|NOT_STARTED` under the
  existing promotion advisory lock and database transition barrier.
- The correction is append-only for terminal epoch history.  It does not
  delete, update, reclassify or retimestamp latency or product evidence.
- The down migration refuses rollback while archived epoch history exists.
- Full unit tests and the complete PostgreSQL 17/18 acceptance matrix prove
  both archival/rearm and the subsequent ordinary Canary lifecycle.
- The final controller binds the migration hashes and invokes the rearm only
  after the root-owned backup has been created and verified.

Unchanged hard boundaries

- Maximum ten REAL SFW Canary sessions.
- At least five valid REAL samples before promotion.
- UNKNOWN provenance fails closed.
- Human acceptance remains DEFERRED.
- Adult media, AVS, payment, external publishing, controlled beta and
  production remain CLOSED.
- Exactly one authoritative Canary/promotion controller; systemd only.

Rollback

The existing controller rollback remains authoritative: verify the root-owned
0700 backup, disable the Canary controller, transition an active Canary to the
fail-closed state, restore the exact predeploy Application/Control commits and
runtime artifacts, restart only the bounded S8/WMS services, then require local
and public health before returning.

